@unsiqasik — thanks for filing this. Same fix as @litaibai2046-debug's [#6618](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/6618), which was posted ~34 minutes earlier (litaibai 15:36 vs your 16:10) and is now merged. Per first-poster precedence, the 50 RTC bounty went to #6618.

No penalty — independently arriving at the same correct fix on a real high-severity bug (arbitrary RTC minting via peer-sync path) is a positive signal. Keep filing.

Tip for avoiding duplicate-work churn: search open issues + recent merges for the file path or function name before opening. `gh pr list --search 'in:title rejects peer-synced'` would have surfaced #6618 immediately.

Reviewed current head `0e6b8da2bfb26bcda32dd4bcc0ac66c2ab9f7ab3`.

Verdict: approve.

What I verified locally on Windows:
- inspected the diff in `node/utxo_db.py` and `node/test_utxo_db.py`;
- `python -m compileall -q node/utxo_db.py node/test_utxo_db.py` passed;
- focused mempool candidate tests passed: `test_mempool_block_candidates`, `test_mempool_block_candidates_limits_sql_scan`, `test_mempool_block_candidates_ignore_expired_transactions`, `test_mempool_block_candidates_drop_spent_inputs`, and `test_mempool_block_candidates_drop_spent_data_inputs`;
- full `PYTHONPATH=node python -m unittest node.test_utxo_db` passed: 96 tests OK;
- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed;
- `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main HEAD` produced a clean tree (`8e492f924ecaf0d97329ed3eb38b56aa06f8e872`).

The change is a targeted fix for the reported DoS class: `mempool_get_block_candidates()` now pushes a bounded `LIMIT ?` into the fee-ordered mempool query instead of materializing every unexpired row before Python applies `max_count`. The regression test confirms the SQL carries the limit and uses the expected overfetch bound for `max_count=1`.

I also checked the `max_count <= 0` edge while reading the function; current code already returns `[]` before computing the scan limit, so the negative/zero limit case is not exposed here.
